WEBVTT

NOTE Captions for the introduction to Every Family Has a Language Plan

1
00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:06.390
Hi, I'm Josh, and this site is called
Every Family Has a Language Plan.

2
00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:13.410
This site is basically a guide for parents,
caregivers, and future parents who are raising

3
00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.230
a child with more than one language.

4
00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:21.070
And even if you've never made a formal plan
before, every family already has one.

5
00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:27.830
It's really just the everyday pattern of who
speaks what language, who they speak

6
00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:30.110
it with, and when they speak it.

7
00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:37.210
This site uses research on family language
policy to help make that pattern much more

8
00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:41.610
intentional without adding to stress
or making the plan too rigid.

9
00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:47.410
On this site, you can learn what the research
says, you can work through some common myths

10
00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:53.290
and misconceptions about bilingual development,
and you can even see examples of how different

11
00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:54.550
families might approach it.

12
00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:58.790
And at the end, come away with a
very simple plan of your own.

13
00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:05.570
By the end, you'll have one reason that the
language matters to your family, one realistic

14
00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:11.410
routine that you can implement this week, one
person who can help you with this plan,

15
00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:15.210
and a date to check in and adjust the plan.

16
00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:19.530
The point of this site is not
to follow a perfect rule.

17
00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:26.730
It's more to create meaningful opportunities
for your child to hear, use, and connect

18
00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:28.450
with this language over time.
